# Word of Command (CR 723.2): "if the chosen card is cast as a spell, you control the player while that spell is
# resolving". On Bot1's turn Bot2 is made to cast Faithless Looting, a sorcery, as Word of Command resolves - at a time a
# sorcery couldn't be cast (CR 608.2g). Word of Command's own control ends as it finishes resolving: while the Looting waits
# on the stack Bot2 is its own (ControlledBy absent, the control waiting as "Bot1+resolving"), and as the Looting resolves
# Bot1 controls Bot2 again and makes its discard choice: Bot2's Lightning Bolt goes, which Bot2 would keep. Once it has
# resolved, no control is left.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Word of Command
Swamp x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Faithless Looting
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x17

[Actions]
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Word of Command.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Faithless Looting)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
? Stack = Faithless Looting
? Bot2.ControlledBy = (absent)
? Bot2.NextTurnControlledBy = Bot1+resolving
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.ControlledBy = Bot1
Bot2.Choose(Lightning Bolt; Mountain)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 3
Bot2.Graveyard.Lightning Bolt.Colors = Red
Bot2.Graveyard.Faithless Looting.Colors = Red
Bot2.Hand.Count = 6
Bot2.ControlledBy = (absent)
Bot2.NextTurnControlledBy = (absent)
